&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we build a global platform for drones and autonomous robots. In the growing market of autonomous vehicles, we connect high-end software and hardware. Our Munich-based defense engineering team develops the technologies that form the foundation of current and future drone products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Electronics Engineer, you will be a member of our interdisciplinary hardware engineering team, driving the design and development of cutting-edge electronics for our next-generation drone platforms. You’ll take ownership of electronic modules such as flight controllers, sensors, and vision systems, leading PCB development from concept to mass production.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of a cross-functional team, you will develop advanced systems such as interceptor and reconnaissance drones with integrated visual navigation, as well as quadcopters for defense applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, prototype, and validate advanced avionics PCBs, sensors, and electronic modules for drone platforms, driving concepts from initial ideation through detailed design and manufacturing readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute comprehensive PCB and product verification activities, including test strategy definition, execution, and documentation; perform electrical and mechanical validation such as EMI/EMC compliance testing, thermal cycling, mechanical shock testing, and HALT analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain technical documentation, including design concepts, schematics and CAD drawings, bills of materials (BOMs), assembly instructions, and repair manuals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with test engineering, manufacturing, and production teams to ensure smooth transition of hardware designs from development to volume production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product management and customer success teams to align system architecture and interfaces, define electronics requirements, and incorporate feedback from field deployments into design improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor junior engineers to achieve technical excellence and develop best practices within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
